    "https://www.fmarion.edu?feed=job_feed&job_types=full-time-faculty%2Cfull-time-staff%2Ctemporary-grant-fte-position%2Cfull-time-temporary-staff%2Cinternal%2Cpart-time-faculty%2Cpart-time-staff%2Cpart-time-temporary-grant-staff%2Ctemp-staff&search_location&job_categories&search_keywords&author": {
      "title": "Full-Time Faculty – Francis Marion University",
      "description": "Full-Time Faculty – Francis Marion University https://www.fmarion.edu Tue, 08 Sep 2026 19:39:28 +0000 en-US hourly 1 https://wordpress.org/?v=7.0.4 https://www.fmarion.edu/wp-content/uploads/2016/07/cropped-Site-Icon-Full-Color-e1502396334483-32x32.png Full-Time Faculty – Francis Marion University https://www.fmarion.edu 32 32 Tenure Track Faculty of Biology and Forestry (26-54) https://www.fmarion.edu/job/tenure-track-faculty-of-biology-and-forestry-26-54/ Brigid Kennedy Tue, 08 Sep 2026 19:37:45 +0000 https://www.fmarion.edu/?post_type=job_listing&p=228516 Francis Marion University and the Departments of Biology and Forestry invite applications for a joint tenure-track Faculty of Biology and Forestry. The successful candidate should be able to teach Wildlife Biology, Conservation Biology, and introductory courses in Biology, Environmental Science and/or Forestry.  There is also opportunity to teach additional classes in the candidate’s area of [&#8230;] <p>Francis Marion University and the Departments of Biology and Forestry invite applications for a joint tenure-track Faculty of Biology and Forestry. The successful candidate should be able to teach Wildlife Biology, Conservation Biology, and introductory courses in Biology, Environmental Science and/or Forestry.  There is also opportunity to teach additional classes in the candidate’s area of expertise.  We are seeking candidates who have a strong commitment to undergraduate teaching and research at a comprehensive liberal arts institution. Other responsibilities include: perform scholarly activities, including mentor undergraduate research projects; serve on department / university committees; provide academic advising for students; participate in additional professional services as needed. The position is a nine-month contract.  Generous internal funding is available on a competitive basis to support travel, research, and undergraduate scholarships.</p>\n<p>Francis Marion University has been recognized for its excellence in education by several national ranking agencies. US News and World Report named FMU as one of its top regional universities in the south for more than a decade. FMU was named as one of ‘The Chronicle’s Great Colleges to Work For’ the past 13 years.</p>\n<p><strong>FMU Requirements:</strong> An earned doctorate in biology, forestry or a closely related discipline from an accredited institution. ABD candidates will be considered but must have completed their degree before their contract starts. Some demonstration of teaching at the undergraduate level is preferred.</p>\n<p><strong>Expected start date:</strong> August 16, 2027</p>\n<p><strong>The following application materials are required</strong>:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Letter of Interest (referencing position number <strong>26-54</strong>).</li>\n<li>Curriculum vitae.</li>\n<li>Teaching Statement expressing teaching experience and philosophy.</li>\n<li>Research Statement describing research interests and long-term research objectives and how the work would involve undergraduate researchers.</li>\n<li>Copies of all transcripts (official transcripts will be required of the successful candidate).</li>\n<li>Names and contact information for at least three references.</li>\n<li>FMU Faculty Application.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>To obtain a Faculty Application please <a href=\"http://www.fmarion.edu/wp-content/uploads/2016/07/FacandOtherSpecApplication7_22_2014ef.pdf\"><strong>click here</strong></a></p>\n<p><strong>Send Application Materials to:</strong></p>\n<p>Dr. Charlene Wages, Vice President for Administration and Planning, Francis Marion University<br />\nP.O. Box 100547, Florence, SC 29502-0547. Or email to: <a href=\"mailto:hrassist@fmarion.edu\">hrassist@fmarion.edu</a>, or  FAX to: (843) 661-1202</p>\n<p><strong>Review of applications will begin on October 12<sup>th</sup>, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>About the Biology Department:</strong> The new faculty member would join a vibrant and collaborative department of 16 faculty who span a wide range of disciplines. We strive for academic excellence within our comprehensive programs using creative teaching, insightful research, and collaborative and impactful service. Faculty in the Biology and Forestry departments have established collaborations with the South Carolina Department of Natural Resources, Forestry Commission, and other state and regional partners, creating opportunities for undergraduate research, experiential learning, and research collaborations. To learn more about Francis Marion University’s Department of Biology, please visit: <a href=\"http://www.fmarion.edu/biology/\">http://www.fmarion.edu/biology/</a>. Any questions may be directed to the Department Chair, Dr. Jeff Steinmetz (<a href=\"mailto:jsteinmetz@fmarion.edu\">jsteinmetz@fmarion.edu</a>) (843) 661-1404.</p>\n<p><strong>About the Forestry Department:</strong> FMU is starting a new forestry program, that seeks to train a new generation of forestry professionals for the sustainable management of forests. The new program is being supported by a number of new faculty hires, a new building currently under construction, and the acquisition of the Duck Ponds Property, an 8355-acre tract along the Great Pee Dee River that will serve as a living laboratory for forestry, environmental science and biology faculty and students.  To learn more about Francis Marion Unviersity’s Forestry Department, please visit: <a href=\"https://www.fmarion.edu/forestry\">https://www.fmarion.edu/forestry</a>. Any questions may be directed to the Forestry Department Chair, Dr. Andrew Londo  (andrew.londo@fmarion.edu) (843) 661-1618.</p>\n<p><strong>About Francis Marion University:</strong> FMU is a state-assisted, regional university comprising over 9100 acres and serving approximately 4,300 students in Florence, SC. FMU is an adamant supporter of academic freedom. The institution takes a strong faculty governance approach with an active AAUP chapter. The campus is within easy driving distance of the state capital Columbia, as well as other areas of interest including Myrtle Beach, Charleston, Charlotte, Asheville, and Savannah. In addition to facilities on the main campus, FMU also owns the Freshwater Ecology Center (FEC), a research facility located 15 minutes from campus with 146 acres of mature hardwood forest and wetlands and a 20-acre lake; and Wildsumaco Biological Station, a field station on the east slope of the Andes in Ecuador, one of several university International Study Centers. Other International Study Centers are located at Rhineland-Palatinate Technical University in Kaiserslautern-Landau, Germany, with a focus on the environment, economics, and politics, and at the University of Prince Edward Island in Charlottetown, Canada, with a focus on environmental sciences and natural resource management.</p>\n<p><strong>About Florence:</strong> Florence, SC, the heart of the Pee Dee region, serves over a quarter million people in the larger metropolitan area. Over the past several years, Florence has experienced major revitalization and rebirth to the downtown area and FMU has been at the forefront of those efforts. In addition to the construction of two health science buildings in the downtown area, we are currently building a medical campus in collaboration with the University of South Carolina Medical School, McLeod Regional Medical Center, and MUSC Health Florence Medical Center. FMU has also contributed to making Florence a center for the arts and culture in the region with the Steven F. Gately Art Gallery and the FMU Performing Arts Center: home to the Florence Symphony Orchestra and hosting many high-profile musical and theatrical performances each year. To find more information about this growing and vibrant community, please visit: <a href=\"https://www.flochamber.com/about-flo/\">https://www.flochamber.com/about-flo/</a>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">As Francis Marion University has continued to be recognized for its diverse student body, it especially welcomes applicants who can affirm and enhance its mission.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">Applicants honorably discharged from a branch of the United States Armed Forces, who meet the minimum training and experience requirements, are given employment preference by all State agencies and higher education institutions in SC.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><em>An Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Institution</em></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"> Forestry and Biology Departments Full-Time Faculty Biology, Forestry Police Officer (26-53) https://www.fmarion.edu/job/police-officer-26-53/ Brigid Kennedy Mon, 24 Aug 2026 12:40:25 +0000 https://www.fmarion.edu/?post_type=job_listing&p=228148 Francis Marion University invites applications from people who want to be part of a team which is directly responsible for the safety of the FMU community.  FMU Police Officers patrol campus and the surrounding community to make them safer, work with students/faculty/staff/visitors to solve problems, conduct educational and community meetings, mediate disputes, investigate traffic collisions, [&#8230;] <p>Francis Marion University invites applications from people who want to be part of a team which is directly responsible for the safety of the FMU community.  FMU Police Officers patrol campus and the surrounding community to make them safer, work with students/faculty/staff/visitors to solve problems, conduct educational and community meetings, mediate disputes, investigate traffic collisions, investigate crimes, make arrests, and provide general police services.</p>\n<p><strong>State Requirements:</strong> A high school diploma and certification by the Law Enforcement Training Council in accordance with §23-23-40 of the Code of Laws of South Carolina 1976.</p>\n<p><strong>FM Preferences:</strong> High school graduate.  The applicant should have an aspiration for personal growth, professional development, and the desire to be a member of a team that maintains a safe campus community.  Required to participate and successfully complete the SC Criminal Justice Academy training if not currently a Class 1 police officer.  Must be 21 years of age or older, have a satisfactory credit report, <strong>a valid SC driver&#8217;s license</strong>, and pass an extensive background investigation which includes a social media review.</p>\n<p><strong>State Classification:</strong> Law Enforcement Officer I (JC10)</p>\n<p><strong>Pay Grade:</strong>LAW03</p>\n<p><strong>Salary:</strong> $49,368</p>\n<p><strong>Normal Working Hours:</strong> Rotating Shifts</p>\n<p><strong>Materials Needed:</strong></p>\n<p>1) Letter of Interest (Referencing Position Number <strong>26-53</strong>).</p>\n<p>2) FMU Staff Application.</p>\n<p>3) Resume.</p>\n<p>4) Copies of all transcripts (official transcripts will be required of the successful candidate).</p>\n<p>5) Valid SC driver&#8217;s license (copy).</p>\n<p>6) 10-Year Motor Vehicle Record from SC Highway Department (original).</p>\n<p>7) Social Security Card (copy).</p>\n<p>8) DD214 (Member &#8211; 4 copy) for Military Services &#8211; if applicable (copy).</p>\n<p>9) Police Officer Certification, if applicable (copy); and</p>\n<p>10) Satisfactory Credit Report (for interviewees only).</p>\n<p><strong> </strong>To obtain the FMU Staff Application, please <a href=\"https://www.fmarion.edu/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Francis-Marion-University-STAFF-Application-v01.25.202261-1.pdf\"><strong>click here.</strong></a></p>\n<p><strong> </strong><strong>Send Application Packet to:</strong> Dr. Charlene Wages, Vice President for Administration, PO Box 100547, Florence, SC 29502-0547 or FAX to (843) 661-1202.</p>\n<p><strong>Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled.</strong></p>\n<p><strong> </strong></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">As Francis Marion University has continued to be recognized for its diverse student body, it especially welcomes applicants who can affirm and enhance its mission.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">Applicants honorably discharged from a branch of the United States Armed Forces, who meet the minimum training and experience requirements, are given employment preference by all State agencies and higher education institutions in SC.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><em>An Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Institution</em></p> Campus Police Full-Time Staff Campus Police Department Custodian-Day Shift (26-52) https://www.fmarion.edu/job/custodian-day-shift-26-52/ Brigid Kennedy Thu, 20 Aug 2026 19:20:31 +0000 https://www.fmarion.edu/?post_type=job_listing&p=228122 Francis Marion University invites applications for a custodian who, under general supervision, performs a variety of routine and complex cleaning and other housekeeping duties. All duties of this position, which is primarily housekeeping, must be performed in accordance with OSHA regulations. Other duties include, but are not limited to: Performing daily cleaning and continuous monitoring [&#8230;] <p>Francis Marion University invites applications for a custodian who, under general supervision, performs a variety of routine and complex cleaning and other housekeeping duties. All duties of this position, which is primarily housekeeping, must be performed in accordance with OSHA regulations.</p>\n<p><strong>Other duties include, but are not limited to:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Performing daily cleaning and continuous monitoring of entrances, stairways, corridors, classrooms, laboratories, and restrooms to maintain a high standard of appearance.</li>\n<li>Performing scheduled cleaning by sweeping, mopping, vacuuming, and dusting in assigned areas including fixtures, furnishings, and equipment.</li>\n<li>Performing specialty cleaning, which includes carpet and vinyl floor cleaning, upholstery cleaning, and window cleaning.</li>\n<li>Ironing fabrics.</li>\n<li>Maintaining assigned custodial closet, maintenance cart, and equipment</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>State Requirements:</strong> Experience in custodial and housekeeping work that is directly related to the area of employment.</p>\n<p><strong>FM Preferences/Requirements:</strong> Knowledge of, or background and ability to learn the operation of, various items of cleaning equipment including vacuums, floor machines, pressure washers, steam-shampoo cleaners, and extractors. Flexibility/strength/stamina to bend, stoop, or lean over, around, or under obstacles while performing work. Must see well enough to read chemical labels accurately in various lighting conditions and to operate equipment safely at normal speeds of production. <strong><em>Should be comfortable around pets.</em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>*A Valid SC Driver&#8217;s License Required. </u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>State Classification:</strong> Building/Grounds Specialist II (KA10)</p>\n<p><strong>Hourly Rate:</strong> $15.74</p>\n<p><em><strong>This full-time position is not a permanent position; however, the duration of employment is expected to be long term.  Furthermore, the staff member will be eligible for all insurance and retirement benefits that are available to permanent employees.</strong></em></p>\n<p><strong>Normal Working Hours:</strong> 8:30am – 5:00 pm (Monday &#8211; Friday). However, hours may vary, and some evening and weekend work may be required. Summer hours will vary.</p>\n<p><strong>Application Procedure:</strong></p>\n<p>Interested applicants may:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Come by the Human Resources Office to complete the application process, or call (843) 661-1140 to have an application mailed; or</li>\n<li>Download the application from our website and either FAX to (843) 661-1202 or mail the requested application referencing Position Number (<strong>26-52</strong>)</li>\n</ol>\n<p>To obtain the FM Staff Application, please <a href=\"https://www.fmarion.edu/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Francis-Marion-University-STAFF-Application-v01.25.202261-1.pdf\"><strong>click here.</strong></a></p>\n<p><strong>Send Application Packet to:</strong> Dr. Charlene Wages, Vice President for Administration and Planning, Francis Marion University, PO Box 100547, Florence, SC 29502-0547 or FAX to (843) 661-1202.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<strong>Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled.</strong></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">\nAs Francis Marion University has continued to be recognized for its diverse student body, it especially welcomes applicants who can affirm and enhance its mission.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">Applicants honorably discharged from a branch of the United States Armed Forces, who meet the minimum training and experience requirements, are given employment preference by all State agencies and higher education institutions in SC.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><em>An Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Institution</em></p> Facilities Full-Time Temporary Staff Custodian Assistant Professor of Biology (26-51) https://www.fmarion.edu/job/assistant-professor-of-biology-26-51/ Brigid Kennedy Tue, 18 Aug 2026 20:36:44 +0000 https://www.fmarion.edu/?post_type=job_listing&p=228072 Francis Marion University and the Department of Biology invite applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Biology. We are seeking candidates who have a strong commitment to undergraduate teaching and research at a comprehensive liberal arts institution. We are open to applications from any discipline, but the candidate must be able to teach introductory biology [&#8230;] <p>Francis Marion University and the Department of Biology invite applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Biology. We are seeking candidates who have a strong commitment to undergraduate teaching and research at a comprehensive liberal arts institution. We are open to applications from any discipline, but the candidate must be able to teach introductory biology as well as human anatomy and/or human physiology.  There is also opportunity to teach additional classes in the candidate’s area of expertise.  Other responsibilities include: perform scholarly activities, including mentor undergraduate research projects; serve on department / university committees; provide academic advising for students; participate in additional professional services as needed. The position is a nine-month contract.  Generous internal funding is available on a competitive basis to support travel, research, and undergraduate scholarship.</p>\n<p><strong>FMU Requirements:</strong> An earned doctorate in biology or a closely related discipline from an accredited institution. ABD candidates will be considered but must have completed their degree before their contract starts. Some demonstration of teaching human anatomy and/or physiology at the undergraduate level is preferred.</p>\n<p><strong>Expected start date:</strong> January 2027.</p>\n<p><strong>The following application materials are required</strong>:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Letter of Interest (referencing position number <strong>26-51</strong>).</li>\n<li>Curriculum vitae.</li>\n<li>Teaching Statement expressing teaching experience and philosophy.</li>\n<li>Research Statement describing research interests and long-term research objectives and how the work would involve undergraduate researchers.</li>\n<li>Copies of all transcripts (official transcripts will be required of the successful candidate).</li>\n<li>Names and contact information for at least three references.</li>\n<li>FMU Faculty Application.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>To obtain a Faculty Application please <a href=\"http://www.fmarion.edu/wp-content/uploads/2016/07/FacandOtherSpecApplication7_22_2014ef.pdf\"><strong>click here</strong></a></p>\n<p><strong>Send Application Materials to:</strong></p>\n<p>Dr. Charlene Wages, Vice President for Administration and Planning, Francis Marion University<br />\nP.O. Box 100547, Florence, SC 29502-0547. Or email to: <a href=\"mailto:hrassist@fmarion.edu\">hrassist@fmarion.edu</a>, or  FAX to: (843) 661-1202</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Review of applications will begin on September 25<sup>th</sup>, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled.</strong></p>\n<p><strong> </strong>Francis Marion University has been recognized for its excellence in education by several national ranking agencies. US News and World Report named FMU as one of its top regional universities in the south for more than a decade. FMU was named as ‘The Chronicle’s Great Colleges to Work For’ the past 13 consecutive years .</p>\n<p><strong> </strong><strong>About the Biology Department:</strong> The new hire would join a vibrant and collaborative department of 17 faculty who span a wide range of disciplines. We strive for academic excellence within our comprehensive programs using creative teaching, insightful research, and collaborative and impactful service. To learn more about Francis Marion University’s Department of Biology, please visit: <a href=\"http://www.fmarion.edu/biology/\">http://www.fmarion.edu/biology/</a>. Any questions regarding this position can be directed to the Department Chair, Dr. Jeff Steinmetz (<a href=\"mailto:jsteinmetz@fmarion.edu\">jsteinmetz@fmarion.edu</a>)</p>\n<p><strong>About Francis Marion University:</strong> FMU is a state-assisted, regional university sitting on over 800 acres and serving approximately 4,200 students in Florence, SC. FMU is an adamant supporter of academic freedom. The institution takes a strong faculty governance approach with an active AAUP chapter. The campus is within easy driving distance of the state capitol Columbia, as well as other areas of interest including Myrtle Beach, Charleston, Charlotte, Asheville, and Savannah. In addition to facilities on the main campus, FMU also owns the Freshwater Ecology Center (FEC), a research facility located 15 minutes from campus with 146 acres of old wood forest and wetlands and a 20-acre lake; the Duck Ponds Property, a 8344 acre tract along the Great Pee Dee River; and Wildsumaco Biological Station, a field station on the east slope of the Andes in Ecuador, one of several university International Study Centers.</p>\n<p><strong>About Florence:</strong> Florence, SC, the heart of the Pee Dee region, serves over a quarter million people in the larger metropolitan area. Over the past several years, Florence has experienced major revitalization and rebirth to the downtown area and FMU has been at the forefront of those efforts. In addition to the construction of two health science buildings in the downtown area, we are currently building a medical campus in collaboration with the University of South Carolina Medical School, McLeod Regional Medical Center, and MUSC Health Florence Medical Center. FMU has also contributed to making Florence a center for the arts and culture in the region with the Steven F. Gately Art Gallery and the FMU Performing Arts Center: home to the Florence Symphony Orchestra and host to many high-profile musical and theatrical performances each year. To find more information about this growing and vibrant community, please visit: <a href=\"https://www.flochamber.com/about-flo/\">https://www.flochamber.com/about-flo/</a>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">As Francis Marion University has continued to be recognized for its diverse student body, it especially welcomes applicants who can affirm and enhance its mission.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">Applicants honorably discharged from a branch of the United States Armed Forces, who meet the minimum training and experience requirements, are given employment preference by all State agencies and higher education institutions in SC.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><em>An Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Institution</em></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p> Leatherman Science Facility Full-Time Faculty Biology Benefits and Leave Coordinator (26-48) https://www.fmarion.edu/job/benefits-and-leave-coordinator-26-48/ Brigid Kennedy Tue, 21 Jul 2026 19:46:13 +0000 https://www.fmarion.edu/?post_type=job_listing&p=227549 Francis Marion University and the Department of Human Resources invite applications for a Benefits and Leave Coordinator who will assist with the creation of personnel records for new staff members; update the records of existing staff; have thorough knowledge of Employee Benefits programs and Leave programs; maintain records and reports associated with each program; understand [&#8230;] <p>Francis Marion University and the Department of Human Resources invite applications for a Benefits and Leave Coordinator who will assist with the creation of personnel records for new staff members; update the records of existing staff; have thorough knowledge of Employee Benefits programs and Leave programs; maintain records and reports associated with each program; understand the <em>Fair Labor Standards Act</em> as it pertains to compensation and classification; and provide professional technical assistance in the coordination of human resource programs in the HR department.</p>\n<p><strong>Other responsibilities include, but are not limited to: </strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Assists the Associate Director of Human Resources-Employee Services with Leave and Benefits Programs, maintenance of staff records, and Worker’s Compensation cases.</li>\n<li>Provides the Associate Director of Human Resources-Administrative Services with the time, leave information necessary to run payroll and complete the required reports.</li>\n<li>Maintains Time Records for all full-time non-exempt employees.</li>\n<li>Conducts orientation to acquaint new staff with agency policies, procedures, and regulations concerning Benefits and Leave.</li>\n<li>Describes insurance and retirement benefits, and other benefits as available, to new and existing employees.</li>\n<li>Discusses eligibility for insurance coverage under the Affordable Care Act.</li>\n<li>Ensures that staff are enrolled in his/her selected programs.</li>\n<li>Assist staff in using websites provided by the Public Employee Benefits Administration.</li>\n<li>Consults with supervisors to ensure that adequate records are maintained for hours worked, and leave used. Provides this information to other HR staff as required.</li>\n<li>Reviews staff leave records with the employee and supervisor, as needed.</li>\n<li>Coordinates with supervisor, employee, and HR staff, if necessary, when situations requiring extended leave arise (e.g., <em>FMLA).</em></li>\n<li>Coordinates with supervisor and staff member&#8211;and HR staff, if necessary—when abuse of leave is suspected.</li>\n<li>Assists in compliance with Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA)  requirements.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Knowledge, Skills and Abilities </strong></p>\n<p><strong> </strong><strong>Required:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Knowledge of Human Resources principles (i.e., hiring, good employee relations, disciplinary practices, end of employment).</li>\n<li>Ability to quickly acquire working knowledge of federal laws and state regulations affecting human resources (<em>FMLA, FLSA, ACA</em>).</li>\n<li>Proficient in Microsoft Office products such as Word, Excel, Outlook and 365.</li>\n<li>Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships.</li>\n<li>Ability to analyze needs and to recommend and communicate solutions effectively.</li>\n<li>Bachelor’s Degree in any field and experience in Human Resources.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><em>Or </em></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Bachelor’s Degree in Human Resources.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><em> </em><em>Applicants without degrees will be considered if they have records of employment which indicate the existence of the requisite knowledge, skills and abilities</em>.</p>\n<p><strong> </strong><strong>Preference:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Experience with an Enterprise Resource Planning software system (e.g. Colleague, Banner, Oracle).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong> </strong><strong>State Classification:</strong>  Human Resources Coordinator (AG07)</p>\n<p><strong>Fed Category:</strong> E2</p>\n<p><strong>Pay Grade: </strong>GEN08</p>\n<p><strong>Salary: </strong>$46,206</p>\n<p><strong>Materials Needed:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Letter of Interest (Referencing Position Number <strong>26-48</strong>).</li>\n<li>Copies of all transcripts (official transcripts will be required of the successful candidate).</li>\n<li>Resume.</li>\n<li>The names, addresses, and telephone numbers of three references; and</li>\n<li>FMU Staff Application.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>To obtain the FMU Staff Application, <a href=\"https://www.fmarion.edu/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Francis-Marion-University-STAFF-Application-v01.25.202261-1.pdf\">please click here.</a></p>\n<p><strong>Send Application Packet to:</strong> Dr. Charlene Wages, Vice President for Administration and Planning, Francis Marion University, PO Box 100547, Florence, SC 29502-0547 or FAX to (843) 661-1202.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled.</strong></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">As Francis Marion University has continued to be recognized for its diverse student body, it especially welcomes applicants who can affirm and enhance its mission.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">Applicants honorably discharged from a branch of the United States Armed Forces, who meet the minimum training and experience requirements, are given employment preference by all State agencies and higher education institutions in SC.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><em>An Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Institution</em></p> Stokes Administration Building Full-Time Staff Human Resources Student Services Coordinator – Admissions (26-46) https://www.fmarion.edu/job/student-services-coordinator-admissions-26-46/ Brigid Kennedy Wed, 01 Jul 2026 20:22:00 +0000 https://www.fmarion.edu/?post_type=job_listing&p=226203 Francis Marion University invites applications for a Student Services Coordinator (Admissions Counselor) who will serve as a primary ambassador of the University and work extensively in the field recruiting and counseling students planning to attend college. Student Services Coordinators spend a significant portion of their time traveling to represent FMU at high schools, college fairs, [&#8230;] <p>Francis Marion University invites applications for a Student Services Coordinator (Admissions Counselor) who will serve as a primary ambassador of the University and work extensively in the field recruiting and counseling students planning to attend college.</p>\n<p>Student Services Coordinators <strong>spend a significant portion of their time traveling</strong> to represent FMU at high schools, college fairs, and community events throughout South Carolina, the Southeast, and other designated recruitment regions. <strong>This position requires frequent day and overnight travel, particularly during peak recruitment seasons, as well as occasional evening and weekend commitments.</strong></p>\n<p>Student Services Coordinators counsel prospective students and families on all aspects of the college selection and enrollment process and consult closely with high school personnel working with potential college students. The Coordinator evaluates and reviews the credentials of prospective freshman and transfer students and serves as a visible, consistent presence in assigned recruitment territories.</p>\n<p>The role involves active participation in recruitment events that <strong>require extensive travel and sustained time on the road</strong>, representing Francis Marion University in a professional and engaging manner.</p>\n<p>Student Services Coordinators advise and counsel students regarding financial assistance, admissions, registration, housing, academic programs, vocational interests, and related areas, both on campus and while traveling throughout their recruitment territory.</p>\n<p><strong>Other responsibilities include, but are not limited to: </strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Recruiting students to FMU through established recruiting protocols, including high school visits, college fairs, telemarketing, campus programs, private visits, and formal presentations.</li>\n<li><strong>Managing an assigned recruitment territory that requires frequent travel</strong>, relationship‑building, and consistent outreach to prospective students and key influencers.</li>\n<li>Evaluating applications of prospective Francis Marion University students.</li>\n<li>Counseling and providing detailed information to prospective students and families about the admissions process, academic programs, and campus support services.</li>\n<li>Maintaining active, on‑going relationships with high school students, counselors, teachers, and administrators, including regular in‑person visits and classroom workshops on college preparation, college life, and career planning.</li>\n<li>Working closely with FMU Alumni to promote the University throughout the community and support recruitment efforts within assigned territories and collaborating with the Director of Admissions to assist students seeking to transfer to FMU.</li>\n<li>Participating in on‑going training to develop the professional skills needed for success in enrollment management, including territory management, recruitment travel planning, and relationship‑based recruitment strategies.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>State Requirement:</strong> A bachelor&#8217;s degree.</p>\n<p><strong>FM Preferences:</strong> A bachelor&#8217;s degree and 1-2 years&#8217; experience in college admissions work, orientation, and event planning is preferred. Knowledge of FMU&#8217;s admission and financial assistance policies and procedures. Knowledge of EMAS and Ellucian software is desired. The ability to travel extensively and work a flexible schedule, with monthly weekend work. <em>Must have a valid Driver’s License</em>. <strong>State Classification:</strong> Student Services Program Coordinator I (CB65)</p>\n<p><strong>Pay Grade: </strong>GEN06</p>\n<p><strong>Salary:</strong> $37,944</p>\n<p><strong>Materials Needed:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Letter of Interest (Referencing Position Number <strong>26-46</strong>).</li>\n<li>Copies of all transcripts (official transcripts will be required of the successful candidate).</li>\n<li>Resume.</li>\n<li>The names, addresses, and telephone numbers of three references; and</li>\n<li>FMU Staff Application.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>To obtain the FMU Staff Application, <a href=\"https://www.fmarion.edu/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Francis-Marion-University-STAFF-Application-v01.25.202261-1.pdf\">please click here.</a></p>\n<p><strong>Send Application Packet to:</strong> Dr. Charlene Wages, Vice President for Administration and Planning, Francis Marion University, PO Box 100547, Florence, SC 29502-0547 or FAX to (843) 661-1202.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled.</strong></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">As Francis Marion University has continued to be recognized for its diverse student body, it especially welcomes applicants who can affirm and enhance its mission.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">Applicants honorably discharged from a branch of the United States Armed Forces, who meet the minimum training and experience requirements, are given employment preference by all State agencies and higher education institutions in SC.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><em>An Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Institution</em></p> Stokes Administration Building Full-Time Staff Admissions Dean of the School of Education (26-43) https://www.fmarion.edu/job/dean-of-the-school-of-education-26-43/ Brigid Kennedy Mon, 08 Jun 2026 17:32:17 +0000 https://www.fmarion.edu/?post_type=job_listing&p=225645 Francis Marion University and the School of Education invite applications for a Dean of the School of Education. The Dean, as the principal advocate for the School of Education, is responsible for the oversight of the School’s academic programs and the cultivation of alumni involvement. The Dean provides leadership that advances the educational and scholarly [&#8230;] <p>Francis Marion University and the School of Education invite applications for a Dean of the School of Education. The Dean, as the principal advocate for the School of Education, is responsible for the oversight of the School’s academic programs and the cultivation of alumni involvement. The Dean provides leadership that advances the educational and scholarly missions of programs in the School and fosters a responsive, student-centered, and innovative academic climate. The Dean is accountable for the review of curricula, accreditation, programs, budget, and all operational functions of the School.  This is a 12-month, full-time administrative appointment, with a reduced teaching load. The Dean is appointed by the President and reports directly to the Provost.</p>\n<p>The School of Education is accredited by the Council for the Accreditation of Educator Preparation (CAEP) and offers a comprehensive portfolio of undergraduate and graduate programs that prepare highly qualified educators to serve South Carolina and the broader region. Undergraduate offerings include Early Childhood Education, Elementary Education, Secondary Education (Biology, English, History, and Mathematics), Art Education, and Special Education/Autism Studies. Graduate programs include Teaching and Learning, Special Education/Multi-Categorical, and accelerated Master of Arts in Teaching pathways. The School maintains strong partnerships with the school districts throughout the Pee Dee, Coastal, and other regions of South Carolina and supports one of the state’s largest Teacher Cadet initiatives. It houses one of 24 South Carolina Teaching Fellows programs, a fellowship program for undergraduate education students, that promotes extensive professional development and service opportunities. The School is also recognized for its Centers of Excellence, including the Center of Excellence for Teaching Children of Poverty and the Center of Excellence for Teacher Retention and Induction in the Pee Dee, reflecting a strong commitment to educational access, student success, and workforce development.</p>\n<p><strong>Required Qualifications:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Terminal degree in an area of scholarly inquiry traditionally associated with the discipline of Education.</li>\n<li>Strong teaching record at the college level.</li>\n<li>Outstanding record of leadership, advocacy, and service to a college, university, and community.</li>\n<li>Successful leadership experience in a department or school of education.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong> </strong><strong>Preferred Qualifications:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Experience in establishing and maintaining effective relationships and connections with public school partners.</li>\n<li>Experience in working collaboratively across academic programs, student affairs, and support services.</li>\n<li>Experience in recruiting, supporting, and retaining a diverse student population.</li>\n<li>An understanding of and commitment to engage first-generation college students.</li>\n<li>Experience in attracting and retaining a diverse and outstanding faculty.</li>\n<li>Evidence of strong communication skills, effective delegating, and a commitment to shared governance.</li>\n<li>A visionary and strategic thinker about schools of education and how they fit into liberal arts university structures and decision-making.</li>\n<li>Classroom experience in the K-12 system.</li>\n<li>Experience with the multifaceted and detailed responsibilities associated with managing and fulfilling the requirements for the Council for the Accreditation of Educator Preparation (CAEP).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Francis Marion University has been recognized for its excellence in education by several national ranking agencies. US News and World Report named FMU as one of its top regional universities in the south for more than a decade. FMU was named as “The Chronicle&#8217;s Great Colleges to Work For” 2013-2026.</p>\n<p>Francis Marion University is a state-assisted, regional, liberal arts university serving approximately 4,200 students in Florence, SC: a growing city with a vibrant culture. The campus is within easy driving distance of the state capitol, Columbia, as well as other areas of interest, including Myrtle Beach, Charleston, Charlotte, Asheville, and Savannah.</p>\n<p>Florence enjoys award winning schools, affordable cost of living, excellent healthcare, and varied recreational programs including sports, community events and festivals.  Florence’s thriving downtown was awarded the prestigious Great American Main Street Award, which recognizes communities for their excellence in comprehensive preservation-based commercial district revitalization.</p>\n<p><strong>Materials Needed: </strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Letter of Interest (Referencing Position Number <strong>26-43</strong>).</li>\n<li>Copies of all transcripts (official transcripts will be required of the successful candidate).</li>\n<li>Curriculum vitae.</li>\n<li>Two letters of recommendation addressing the candidate’s qualifications for the position.</li>\n<li>Applicants may also submit the name, title, mailing address, email address, and telephone numbers of additional professional references.</li>\n<li>FMU Faculty Application.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>To obtain a copy of the faculty application, please <a href=\"http://www.fmarion.edu/wp-content/uploads/2016/07/FacandOtherSpecApplication7_22_2014ef.pdf\"><strong>click here.</strong></a></p>\n<p><strong>Send complete application packet to</strong>: Dr. Charlene Wages, Vice President for Administration and Planning, Francis Marion University, P.O. Box 100547, Florence, SC 29502-0547. May also be submitted via fax at 843-661-1202 or email to: HRAssist@fmarion.edu</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong> </strong>As Francis Marion University has continued to be recognized for its diverse student body, it especially welcomes applicants who can affirm and enhance its mission.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">Applicants honorably discharged from a branch of the United States Armed Forces, who meet the minimum training and experience requirements, are given employment preference by all State agencies and higher education institutions in South Carolina.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><em>An Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Institution</em></p> School of Education Full-Time Faculty School of Education Teaching Assistant (26-34) https://www.fmarion.edu/job/teaching-assistant-26-34/ Brigid Kennedy Tue, 10 Mar 2026 19:25:39 +0000 https://www.fmarion.edu/?post_type=job_listing&p=163619 Francis Marion University and the Gail &#38; Terry Richardson Center for the Child invite applications for a Teaching Assistant to serve as a floater and assist where needed. Duties include, but are not limited to: Assists the Lead Teacher in planning both long and short-range activities in accordance with curriculum objectives, developmentally appropriate practice and [&#8230;] <p>Francis Marion University and the Gail &amp; Terry Richardson Center for the Child invite applications for a Teaching Assistant to serve as a floater and assist where needed.</p>\n<p><strong>Duties include, but are not limited to: </strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Assists the Lead Teacher in planning both long and short-range activities in accordance with curriculum objectives, developmentally appropriate practice and program philosophy.</li>\n<li>Manage the classroom routine in the absence of the Lead Teacher.</li>\n<li>Assists the Lead Teacher in meeting the emotional, social, physical and cognitive needs of each child.</li>\n<li>Assists the Lead Teacher in arranging a classroom environment in accordance with program goals and philosophy.</li>\n<li>Assists the Lead Teacher in maintaining a safe and healthy environment.</li>\n<li>Assists the Lead Teacher in maintaining anecdotal records.</li>\n<li>Maintains confidentiality.</li>\n<li>Completes professional development activities in early childhood education through in-service training and/or college level courses.</li>\n<li>Maintains all applicable licensing regulations.</li>\n<li>Maintains certification in Infant/Child First Aid and CPR.</li>\n<li>All other duties assigned by the director.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Educational Requirements:</strong> A high school diploma required.  An Early Childhood Credential or Two-Year Degree as a Child Development Associate (CDA) is preferred.  Experience in education, child care or general administration in working with Infants, Toddlers, Two, Three and Four-Year Old children preferred.</p>\n<p><strong>NOTE: THIS IS A TEMPORARY POSITION AND IS NOT COVERED BY THE STATE GRIEVANCE POLICY.</strong>  The position will depend upon the needs of the Center but is expected that the need for this position will be continuous.  The only benefit available is participation in the State retirement system.</p>\n<p><strong>Hourly Rate:</strong> $15.00/hour</p>\n<p><strong>Typical Work Schedule:</strong> Hours may vary (based on need), but approximately 25 hours/week.</p>\n<p><strong>Physical Requirements:</strong> Must have the ability to bend, twist, squat, kneel, climb, reach above shoulder, grip/grasp, extend/flex neck, use right hand, use left hand, ability to see, lift up to 40 lbs., stand, walk, sit, drive, perform repetitive hand motions, and the ability to hear.</p>\n<p><strong>Materials needed:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Letter of Interest (Referencing Position Number <strong>26-34</strong>).</li>\n<li>FMU Staff Application.</li>\n<li>Resume.</li>\n<li>Three letters of reference with addresses, with both personal and work telephone numbers.</li>\n<li>Copy of SC Driver’s License.</li>\n<li>Copy of High School Diploma, GED, or Certificate of Completion.</li>\n<li>Copy of Diploma for CDA or Early Childhood Credential, if applicable.</li>\n<li>Copy of transcript from institution granting the Early Childhood Credential or two-year degree (official transcript will be required of the successful candidate).</li>\n</ol>\n<p>To obtain the FMU Staff Application, please <a href=\"https://www.fmarion.edu/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Francis-Marion-University-STAFF-Application-v01.25.202261-1.pdf\"><strong>click here</strong>.</a></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">The successful candidate must complete all DSS required forms, which include the completion of a State and Federal background check and related health assessment/medical statements.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>No offer can be made until the process has been completed.</strong></p>\n<p><strong> </strong><strong>Send complete application packet to:</strong> Dr. Charlene Wages, Vice President for Administration and Planning, Francis Marion University, P.O. Box 100547, Florence, SC 29502-0547.  May also be submitted via fax at 843-661-1202</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">As Francis Marion University has continued to be recognized for its diverse student body, it especially welcomes applicants who can affirm and enhance its mission.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">Applicants honorably discharged from a branch of the United States Armed Forces, who meet the minimum training and experience requirements, are given employment preference by all State agencies and higher education institutions in South Carolina.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><em>An Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Institution</em></p> Richardson Center for the Child Temporary Staff Gail and Terry Richardson Center for the Child Pre-School Lead Teacher (26-33) https://www.fmarion.edu/job/pre-school-lead-teacher-26-33/ Brigid Kennedy Tue, 10 Mar 2026 19:16:49 +0000 https://www.fmarion.edu/?post_type=job_listing&p=163613 Gail and Terry Richardson Center for the Child Francis Marion University invites applications for a Pre-school teacher, serving ages 3-5. for the Gail and Terry Richardson Center for the Child (RCC) at Francis Marion University.  Plans and implements educational programs for the Child Care facility.  Plans both long- and short-range activities in accordance with curriculum [&#8230;] <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Gail and Terry Richardson Center for the Child </strong></p>\n<p>Francis Marion University invites applications for a Pre-school teacher, serving ages 3-5. for the Gail and Terry Richardson Center for the Child (RCC) at Francis Marion University.  Plans and implements educational programs for the Child Care facility.  Plans both long- and short-range activities in accordance with curriculum objectives, developmentally appropriate practice, and program philosophy.  Develops programs for young children based on current knowledge of child development and early childhood education.  Ensures all programs and activities fit the training, research, and service needs of the Center for the Child and University community.  Works closely with the various academic departments as the RCC also serves as a training facility for FMU students in early childhood education, psychology, nursing, speech language pathology, occupation therapy and is a site for research and community services.</p>\n<p><strong>Duties</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Plan both long- and short-range activities in accordance with curriculum objectives, developmentally appropriate practice and program philosophy.</li>\n<li>Meet the emotional, social, physical, and cognitive needs of each child.</li>\n<li>Encourage assistants to contribute to curriculum planning.</li>\n<li>Coordinate on campus field trips.</li>\n<li>Prepare monthly plan charts.</li>\n<li>Complete bi-annual assessment of children’s development.</li>\n<li>Report progress of children to parents in bi-annual reports and through parent-teacher conferences.</li>\n<li>Maintain daily open communication with parents.</li>\n<li>Keep accident reports.</li>\n<li>Maintain anecdotal records.</li>\n<li>Maintains confidentiality.</li>\n<li>Report any suspected abuse to supervisor and the Department of Social Services.</li>\n<li>Arrange a classroom environment in accordance to program goals and philosophy.</li>\n<li>Maintain a safe and healthy environment.</li>\n<li>Inspect and replace damaged or lost materials.</li>\n<li>Attend in-service and staff meetings.</li>\n<li>Supervise assistants, aides, and volunteers in the classroom.</li>\n<li>Keep all appropriate records such as records, attendance, and time sheets.</li>\n<li>Meet all applicable licensing regulations.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong> </strong><strong>FMU Requirements and Preferences:</strong>  A bachelor&#8217;s degree required.  Must be certified in Early Childhood Education.  Experience in education, childcare or general administration in working with Infants, Toddlers, Twos/Threes, or Four-year old children preferred.</p>\n<p><strong>Normal Working Hours:</strong>  37.5 hours/week.  (10.75-month contract, renewable year-to-year.)</p>\n<p><strong>Salary:</strong> $36,000</p>\n<p><strong>Start Date:</strong> As soon as possible.</p>\n<p><strong>Physical Requirements:</strong>  Must have the ability to bend, twist, squat, kneel, climb, reach above shoulder, grip/grasp, extend/flex neck, use right hand, use left hand, ability to see, lift to 40 lbs, stand, walk, sit, drive, perform repetitive hand motions, keyboarding/mouse work, and the ability to hear.</p>\n<p><strong>Materials Needed</strong>:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Letter of interest (referencing Position Numbers <strong>26-33</strong>).</li>\n<li>Resume.</li>\n<li>Copy of all College transcripts. (Official college transcripts will be required of the successful   candidate).</li>\n</ol>\n<ol start=\"4\">\n<li>Three letters of reference with addresses, home and work telephone numbers.</li>\n<li>Copy of SC Driver’s License.</li>\n<li>Copy of High School Diploma or GED.</li>\n<li>Copy of College Diploma.</li>\n<li>FMU Application.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>To obtain the FM Staff Application, please <a href=\"https://www.fmarion.edu/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Francis-Marion-University-STAFF-Application-v01.25.202261-1.pdf\"><strong>click here.</strong></a></p>\n<p><strong> </strong><strong>Send Application Packet to</strong>:  Dr. Charlene Wages, Vice President for Administration &amp; Planning, Francis Marion University, PO Box 100547, Florence, SC 29502-0547 or fax information to (843) 661-1202. Or via email; HRAssist@fmarion.edu</p>\n<p><strong>The successful candidate must complete all DSS required forms:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>A Consent to Release Information form</li>\n<li>Evidence of Non-Conviction and Statement of Compliance</li>\n<li>Verification of experience working in a Child Care Facility (a written statement from each childcare stating the center’s name, address, telephone number, A/L/R number and employee’s dates of employment is required.)</li>\n<li>Medical Statement</li>\n<li>A copy of current Infant/Child CPR and First Aid Card, if applicable</li>\n<li>Completion of State background check</li>\n<li>Completion of Federal background check</li>\n<li>Related health assessment/medical statement</li>\n</ol>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled.</strong></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"> As Francis Marion University has continued to be recognized for its diverse student body, it especially welcomes applicants who can affirm and enhance its mission.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">Applicants honorably discharged from a branch of the United States Armed Forces, who meet the minimum training and experience requirements, are given employment preference by all State agencies and higher education institutions in SC.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><em>An Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Institution</em></p> Richardson center for the Child Full-Time Staff Gail and Terry Richardson Center for the Child Director of Testing, Counseling, and Special Services Center  (26-30) https://www.fmarion.edu/job/director-of-testing-counseling-and-special-services-center-26-30/ Brigid Kennedy Mon, 16 Feb 2026 13:28:59 +0000 https://www.fmarion.edu/?post_type=job_listing&p=163349 Francis Marion University invites applications for a Director of Testing, Counseling, and Special Services Center.  TCSS is the primary provider of mental health services for FMU students.  It provides services to help students cope with college and life pressures that threaten persistence in college and to develop or enhance skills that optimize personal effectiveness. Faculty and [&#8230;] <p>Francis Marion University invites applications for a Director of Testing, Counseling, and Special Services Center.  TCSS is the primary provider of mental health services for FMU students.  It provides services to help students cope with college and life pressures that threaten persistence in college and to develop or enhance skills that optimize personal effectiveness. Faculty and staff may also seek short-term consultation.  Additionally, the center arranges for the administration of exams that require accommodation for standardized tests.</p>\n<p><strong>Responsibilities include but are not limited to:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Develop long-range plans and objectives for the TCSS</li>\n<li>Consult with supervisor to develop and monitor budgets for the TCSS</li>\n<li>Work with the University community to ensure timely response to counseling services</li>\n<li>Provide screening, assessment, and counseling services to University students</li>\n<li>Consult with students to identify services which will allow them to accommodate for conditions that interfere with the activities of daily living:\n<ul>\n<li>Review records to determine if the student is eligible for ADA accommodations</li>\n<li>Meet with students to identify reasonable accommodations</li>\n<li>Communicate with faculty and staff to ensure the accommodations are implemented</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Serve as liaison between Francis Marion University and SC Vocational Rehabilitation services</li>\n<li>Provide training and supervision for students enrolled in FMU graduate programs:</li>\n<li>Master of Science in Applied Psychology &#8211; Clinical/Counseling Program.</li>\n<li>Doctor of Psychology Program</li>\n<li>Coordinate fee-based administration of standardized tests for prospective and current students and external users</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong> </strong><strong>FMU Requirements:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Doctoral Degree in Psychology</li>\n<li>Licensure or ability to be licensed as a Licensed Psychologist or Licensed Professional Counselor in South Carolina</li>\n<li>Excellent oral and written communication skills</li>\n<li>Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships</li>\n<li>Knowledge in psychological theory, assessment, and practice techniques</li>\n<li>Knowledge of psychological and educational outreach needs of college students</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong> </strong><strong>FMU Preferences:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Counseling experience in a higher education setting</li>\n<li>Knowledge of alcohol and other drug counseling techniques, intervention strategies</li>\n<li>Experience in working with culturally diverse population.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>State Requirements: </strong>A master&#8217;s degree and professional experience in a human service or social service program.<strong><br />\nState Classification:</strong> Human Services Coordinator III (GA70)</p>\n<p><strong>Pay Grade:</strong> GEN10</p>\n<p><strong>Salary:</strong> Commensurate with SC pay grades, qualifications, and experience.<strong> </strong></p>\n<p><strong> </strong><strong>Materials Needed:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Letter of Interest (Referencing Position Number <strong>26-30</strong>).</li>\n<li>Copies of all transcripts (official transcripts will be required of the successful candidate).</li>\n<li>Copies of all licenses and related certifications.</li>\n<li>Resume.</li>\n<li>The names, addresses (both mail and email), and telephone numbers of three references, and;</li>\n<li>FM Staff Application.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>To obtain the FM Staff Application, please <a href=\"https://www.fmarion.edu/wp-content/uploads/2016/07/FMU-Staff-Application-v042226-PDF.pdf\">click here.</a></p>\n<p><strong>Send Application Packet to:</strong> Dr. Charlene Wages, Vice President for Administration and Planning, Francis Marion University, PO Box 100547, Florence, SC 29502-0547 or FAX to (843) 661-1202.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled.</strong></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">As Francis Marion University has continued to be recognized for its diverse student body, it especially welcomes applicants who can affirm and enhance its mission.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">Applicants honorably discharged from a branch of the United States Armed Forces, who meet the minimum training and experience requirements, are given employment preference by all State agencies and higher education institutions in SC.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><em>An Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Institution</em></p> Testing, Counseling, and Special Services Center Full-Time Staff Testing, Counseling, and Special Services Center"
