    "https://www.fmarion.edu/job/custodian-day-shift-26-52/": {
      "title": "Custodian-Day Shift (26-52)",
      "description": "Custodian-Day Shift (26-52) - Francis Marion University Potential Students Campus Tours and Maps Campus Map Student Life Accounting for Students Apply Now Dining Services Financial Assistance Graduate Programs Honors Housing International Programs Majors Scholarships Visit Registrar Current Students Student Resources Blackboard Campus Technology CASA Career Center CASA Advising Tutoring Center Writing Center Testing, Counseling, & Special Services Center Dining Services Disability Services Purchase Textbooks Rogers Library Ombudsman Student Handbook Student Services and Documents Registrar’s Office Accounting Bookstore Calendar Course Catalogs Directory Financial Assistance Honors Housing Patriot Gear Patriot Marketplace Registrar Scholarships Student Employment Student Life SwampFox Alerts Alumni Alumni Gear Give Donate Homecoming Join News Alumni Magazine Community Calendar Campus Tours and Maps Evening College Facility Rental Foundation & Development Economic Development Education Foundation Freshwater Ecology Complex Gately Gallery Hewn Timber Cabins Kelley Center Performing Arts Center Regional & Community Programs Richardson Center for the Child Dooley Planetarium University Communications FOIA Requests Faculty/Staff African American Faculty & Staff Coalition Blackboard Calendar Campus Technology Career Opportunities Directory Email Facilities Management Space Reservation Faculty Handbook Grants Human Resources Employment Opportunities Policies Library Performing Arts Center Richardson Center for the Child SwampFox Alerts Patriot Portal Password Management- Reset & Recovery Portal 101 Portal Login Proxy Login Authorized User Login Career Opportunities Menu APPLY Apply to FMU Apply Now ABOUT History, Facts President Campus Tours and Maps Administration Policies Human Resources Facilities Management Financial Services & Budget Office University Communications Registrar General Counsel Foundation & Development Institutional Research Staff Awards Faculty/Staff Directory FMU Organizational Chart Governance Board of Trustees Faculty Governance Student Government Association Calendar ACADEMICS Programs, Majors College of Liberal Arts School of Business School of Health Sciences School of Education FMU’s Evening College Graduate Programs Library Honors International Programs McNair Scholars Program Provost Accreditation Continuity of Instruction Deans & Department Chairs Institutional Review Board Student Success Academic Catalog Academic Resources Research Registrar ADMISSIONS Apply, Financial Aid Apply Now Requirements Campus Visit Open House Financial Assistance Scholarships Net Price Calculator Accepted Students Orientation Honors Graduate Programs Dual Enrollment School Counselors Request Information ATHLETICS Sports, Events STUDENT LIFE Activities, Events Activities & Organizations Student Health Greek Life Ms. FMU Housing Custodian-Day Shift (26-52) Home job August 20, 2026 Custodian-Day Shift (26-52) Full-Time Temporary Staff Facilities Posted 3 weeks ago Francis Marion University invites applications for a custodian who, under general supervision, performs a variety of routine and complex cleaning and other housekeeping duties. All duties of this position, which is primarily housekeeping, must be performed in accordance with OSHA regulations. Other duties include, but are not limited to: Performing daily cleaning and continuous monitoring of entrances, stairways, corridors, classrooms, laboratories, and restrooms to maintain a high standard of appearance. Performing scheduled cleaning by sweeping, mopping, vacuuming, and dusting in assigned areas including fixtures, furnishings, and equipment. Performing specialty cleaning, which includes carpet and vinyl floor cleaning, upholstery cleaning, and window cleaning. Ironing fabrics. Maintaining assigned custodial closet, maintenance cart, and equipment State Requirements: Experience in custodial and housekeeping work that is directly related to the area of employment. FM Preferences/Requirements: Knowledge of, or background and ability to learn the operation of, various items of cleaning equipment including vacuums, floor machines, pressure washers, steam-shampoo cleaners, and extractors. Flexibility/strength/stamina to bend, stoop, or lean over, around, or under obstacles while performing work. Must see well enough to read chemical labels accurately in various lighting conditions and to operate equipment safely at normal speeds of production. Should be comfortable around pets. *A Valid SC Driver’s License Required. State Classification: Building/Grounds Specialist II (KA10) Hourly Rate: $15.74 This full-time position is not a permanent position; however, the duration of employment is expected to be long term.  Furthermore, the staff member will be eligible for all insurance and retirement benefits that are available to permanent employees. Normal Working Hours: 8:30am – 5:00 pm (Monday – Friday). However, hours may vary, and some evening and weekend work may be required. Summer hours will vary. Application Procedure: Interested applicants may: Come by the Human Resources Office to complete the application process, or call (843) 661-1140 to have an application mailed; or Download the application from our website and either FAX to (843) 661-1202 or mail the requested application referencing Position Number ( 26-52 ) To obtain the FM Staff Application, please click here. Send Application Packet to: Dr. Charlene Wages, Vice President for Administration and Planning, Francis Marion University, PO Box 100547, Florence, SC 29502-0547 or FAX to (843) 661-1202. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. As Francis Marion University has continued to be recognized for its diverse student body, it especially welcomes applicants who can affirm and enhance its mission. Applicants honorably discharged from a branch of the United States Armed Forces, who meet the minimum training and experience requirements, are given employment preference by all State agencies and higher education institutions in SC. An Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Institution August 20, 2026 | | APPLY Ready to start your FMU journey? Apply now CONTACT Get in touch with a friendly FMU representative. VISIT Schedule an in-person tour or View the Campus map here . DONATE Give the gift of opportunity to a Francis Marion Patriot here. IMPORTANT LINKS FMU Safe Campus Tucker Hipps Report Title IX & Discrimination Policies Clery Report Transparency Reports Student Achievement & Success Website Privacy GDPR Policy Campus Map Accreditation UNIVERSITY HONORS U.S. News & World Report Best Social Mobility U.S. News & World Report Best Regional University South U.S. News & World Report Top Public University U.S. News & World Report Top Performer Economic Diversity U.S. News & World Report Top Business & Engineering Schools TOP © 2026 Francis Marion University | 4822 E. Palmetto St., Florence, S.C. 29506 | PO Box 100547, Florence, S.C. 29502 APPLY Apply Now ABOUT President Campus Tours and Maps Administration Policies Human Resources Facilities Management Financial Services & Budget Office University Communications Registrar General Counsel Foundation & Development Institutional Research Staff Awards Faculty/Staff Directory FMU Organizational Chart Governance Board of Trustees Faculty Governance Student Government Association Calendar ACADEMICS College of Liberal Arts School of Business School of Health Sciences School of Education FMU’s Evening College Graduate Programs Library Honors International Programs McNair Scholars Program Provost Accreditation Continuity of Instruction Deans & Department Chairs Institutional Review Board Student Success Academic Catalog Academic Resources Research Registrar ADMISSIONS Apply Now Requirements Campus Visit Open House Financial Assistance Scholarships Net Price Calculator Accepted Students Orientation Honors Graduate Programs Dual Enroll