evelopment Institutional Research Staff Awards Faculty/Staff Directory FMU Organizational Chart Governance Board of Trustees Faculty Governance Student Government Association Calendar ACADEMICS Programs, Majors College of Liberal Arts School of Business School of Health Sciences School of Education FMU’s Evening College Graduate Programs Library Honors International Programs McNair Scholars Program Provost Accreditation Continuity of Instruction Deans & Department Chairs Institutional Review Board Student Success Academic Catalog Academic Resources Research Registrar ADMISSIONS Apply, Financial Aid Apply Now Requirements Campus Visit Open House Financial Assistance Scholarships Net Price Calculator Accepted Students Orientation Honors Graduate Programs Dual Enrollment School Counselors Request Information ATHLETICS Sports, Events STUDENT LIFE Activities, Events Activities & Organizations Student Health Greek Life Ms. FMU Housing Director of Testing, Counseling, and Special Services Center  (26-30) Home job February 16, 2026 Director of Testing, Counseling, and Special Services Center  (26-30) Full-Time Staff Testing, Counseling, and Special Services Center Posted 7 months ago Francis Marion University invites applications for a Director of Testing, Counseling, and Special Services Center.  TCSS is the primary provider of mental health services for FMU students.  It provides services to help students cope with college and life pressures that threaten persistence in college and to develop or enhance skills that optimize personal effectiveness. Faculty and staff may also seek short-term consultation.  Additionally, the center arranges for the administration of exams that require accommodation for standardized tests. Responsibilities include but are not limited to: Develop long-range plans and objectives for the TCSS Consult with supervisor to develop and monitor budgets for the TCSS Work with the University community to ensure timely response to counseling services Provide screening, assessment, and counseling services to University students Consult with students to identify services which will allow them to accommodate for conditions that interfere with the activities of daily living: Review records to determine if the student is eligible for ADA accommodations Meet with students to identify reasonable accommodations Communicate with faculty and staff to ensure the accommodations are implemented Serve as liaison between Francis Marion University and SC Vocational Rehabilitation services Provide training and supervision for students enrolled in FMU graduate programs: Master of Science in Applied Psychology – Clinical/Counseling Program. Doctor of Psychology Program Coordinate fee-based administration of standardized tests for prospective and current students and external users FMU Requirements: Doctoral Degree in Psychology Licensure or ability to be licensed as a Licensed Psychologist or Licensed Professional Counselor in South Carolina Excellent oral and written communication skills Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships Knowledge in psychological theory, assessment, and practice techniques Knowledge of psychological and educational outreach needs of college students FMU Preferences: Counseling experience in a higher education setting Knowledge of alcohol and other drug counseling techniques, intervention strategies Experience in working with culturally diverse population. State Requirements: A master’s degree and professional experience in a human service or social service program. State Classification: Human Services Coordinator III (GA70) Pay Grade: GEN10 Salary: Commensurate with SC pay grades, qualifications, and experience. Materials Needed: Letter of Interest (Referencing Position Number 26-30 ). Copies of all transcripts (official transcripts will be required of the successful candidate). Copies of all licenses and related certifications. Resume. The names, addresses (both mail and email), and telephone numbers of three references, and; FM Staff Application. To obtain the FM Staff Application, please click here. Send Application Packet to: Dr. Charlene Wages, Vice President for Administration and Planning, Francis Marion University, PO Box 100547, Florence, SC 29502-0547 or FAX to (843) 661-1202. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. As Francis Marion University has continued to be recognized for its diverse student body, it especially welcomes applicants who can affirm and enhance its mission. Applicants honorably discharged from a branch of the United States Armed Forces, who meet the minimum training and experience requirements, are given employment preference by all State agencies and higher education institutions in SC. An Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Institution February 16, 2026 | | APPLY Ready to start your FMU journey? Apply now CONTACT Get in touch with a friendly FMU representative. VISIT Schedule an in-person tour or View the Campus map here . DONATE Give the gift of opportunity to a Francis Marion Patriot here. IMPORTANT LINKS FMU Safe Campus Tucker Hipps Report Title IX & Discrimination Policies Clery Report Transparency Reports Student Achievement & Success Website Privacy GDPR Policy Campus Map Accreditation UNIVERSITY HONORS U.S. News & World Report Best Social Mobility U.S. News & World Report Best Regional University South U.S. News & World Report Top Public University U.S. News & World Report Top Performer Economic Diversity U.S. News & World Report Top Business & Engineering Schools TOP © 2026 Francis Marion University | 4822 E. Palmetto St., Florence, S.C. 29506 | PO Box 100547, Florence, S.C. 29502 APPLY Apply Now ABOUT President Campus Tours and Maps Administration Policies Human Resources Facilities Management Financial Services & Budget Office University Communications Registrar General Counsel Foundation & Development Institutional Research Staff Awards Faculty/Sta